  "description": "Rung 3: a member who has never won is measured from their join date, not treated as infinitely overdue, so a brand-new member does not jump the queue",
  "spec_clause": "Phase 2 / Tally rung 3: 'Measure members who have never won from their join date, not as infinitely overdue - otherwise someone who joined yesterday jumps the entire queue.'",
  "rationale": "3 attendees, two finalists. u2 joined on 2026-07-01 (four weeks ago) and has never had a winning suggestion; u1 last won on 2026-02-01. m1 is suggested by u1, m2 by u2. Phase 1: m1 rows u1,u2 yes / u3 no -> coverage 3/3 = 1.00, yes 2, approval 2/3 = 0.6667; m2 rows u1,u3 yes / u2 no -> yes 2, approval 0.6667. Both promoted (tie away from the boundary). Runoff: the single pair m1 vs m2 is 1 (u1) to 1 (u2), with u3 recording an explicit no preference that counts for neither side -> 1-1, no pair winner. Copeland 0-0 -> tie, no Condorcet winner. Approval 0.6667 = 0.6667 -> tie. Rung 3 rotation fairness: waiting_since(u1) = last_win_at = 2026-02-01; waiting_since(u2) = joined_at = 2026-07-01 because he has never won. 2026-02-01 is earlier, so u1 has gone longer without a winning suggestion -> winner m1. Treating 'never won' as infinitely overdue would wrongly hand the win to the newest member's suggestion m2.",
